I think it would be funny if pets had an arbitrary skill which the player
didn't know about until the pet was seen exercising the skill. 

If the pet had a valuable skill such as unlocking doors or trunks, or
finding food the player would go out of his/her way to keep the pet alive.
However, if the pet had a negative skill such as stealing and disappearing
with food, or locking doors it would be ditched ASAP.

These would be rare skill attributes to the pet, maybe 1 in 30 pets would
generate with the flag (enough so that in a full game you might find one or
two) and they would have various levels of the skill which they could
exercise.

I think that having a cat bring a starving wizard food or a dog opening the
doors in soko for a tourist would be really cool.




